(1) A maintenance business entity outsourced to conduct safety inspections or emergency safety inspections of establishments in accordance with the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have registered as an institution specializing in safety inspections under the amended provisions of Article 28-2; provided, it shall make a new registration within 1 year from the date this Act enters into force, after meeting the registration standards under the amended provisions of Article 28-2.
(2) A maintenance business entity under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force may continue to perform tasks only for the agency contracts for safety inspections, emergency safety inspections, or maintenance for establishments concluded before this Act enters into force.
(3) Acts done by or toward a maintenance business entity outsourced to conduct safety inspections or emergency safety inspections of establishments in accordance with the previous provisions before this Act enters into force shall be deemed acts done by or toward an institution specializing safety inspections registered in accordance with the amended provisions of Article 28-2 after this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning administrative dispositions)
The previous provisions shall apply to administrative dispositions applied for violations committed before this Act enters into force.

